      "message": "The combined logic above this point is roughly 1.1 seconds, with about half of that time coming between b2/b3 and half between b3/c.\n\nMost of the time in both of these blocks is spent in calls to `trng_init` and `trng_rand`\n\n```\n2023-07-29T00:11:22.468000Z [34.871652 HC 0x0404]\n2023-07-29T00:11:22.468000Z [34.871965 fp_frame time(a): 3\n2023-07-29T00:11:22.468000Z ]\n2023-07-29T00:11:22.468000Z [34.872019 fp_frame time(b): 57\n2023-07-29T00:11:22.468000Z ]\n2023-07-29T00:11:22.468000Z [34.872074 fp_frame time(b1): 112\n2023-07-29T00:11:22.468000Z ]\n2023-07-29T00:11:22.468000Z [34.872174 fp_frame time(b2): 212\n2023-07-29T00:11:22.468000Z ]\n2023-07-29T00:11:23.019000Z [35.423362 fp_frame time(b3): 551401\n2023-07-29T00:11:23.019000Z ]\n2023-07-29T00:11:23.569000Z [35.972659 fp_frame time(c): 1100697\n2023-07-29T00:11:23.569000Z ]\n2023-07-29T00:11:23.569000Z [35.972771 Seed hasn\u0027t been set.]\n2023-07-29T00:11:23.569000Z [35.972819 Failed to get IKM: 7]\n2023-07-29T00:11:23.569000Z [35.972901 fgr0: Failed to derive key]\n2023-07-29T00:11:23.569000Z [35.972962 HC 0x0404 err 9]\n```\n\nAccording to the datasheet we should be able to pull about 2500 random bytes per second. From what I can see here we\u0027re calculating 12 (`FP_CONTEXT_NONCE_BYTES`) + 16 (`FP_CONTEXT_ENCRYPTION_SALT_BYTES`) in the b2-b3 block and 16 (`FP_POSITIVE_MATCH_SALT_BYTES`) in the b3-c block. Are we not providing enough entropy? Is there a better API for that?",
